#4471 combined reports that do not all describe the same problem. The counts below are based on the export through 4 October, not a live queue. They count each report ID once.

## Problems and tickets

<ReportSplit />

The parser reads month first even for day-first tenants. The booking-v3 form, separately, shows a month-first hint while interpreting the entry in the tenant's format. Intake tags are guesses, not a reliable way to split these reports.

Five reports flagged in the desk notes describe a one-day move. They were assigned to the parser group by tenant, but their symptoms warrant a separate investigation. Their root cause is not established. They are excluded from the parser count above so no report is counted twice.

## What to do next

Check the live desk before relying on this snapshot: reports may have arrived or been refiled since the export. Compare symptoms and tenant details, not just matching subjects. The older [triage rule](/kb/triage/dedupe) and [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) describe subject-based merging; do not silently rewrite the accepted decision.

Sources: the [original incident](/kb/incidents/4471), `reports-4471.json`, `desk-notes.json`, tenant records, and `causes.ts` in this export.

